{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794425451,"nonce":"0MBU5aEDVio/Ckp0oOkUQk/+tRw=","title":"Reported 2026-11-12 from the devops-gitops pilot on Scarab 0.3.2.","message":"Triggers cannot filter on changed files. An `on:` trigger's `when:` is CEL over the event (`Event::context`, crates/scarab-forge/src/lib.rs ~643): kind, repo, ref, branch, sha, tag, number, fork, issue, comment body, schedule. There is no changed-files field, so a Pipeline that builds an image for one directory either runs on every push and PR or is manual-only.\n\nProposed: `event.changed_paths`, a list of repository paths, readable in `when:` only (it is free text, so not in `event.rs` `READABLE` for templates):\n\n    on:\n      push:\n        when: event.changed_paths.exists(p, p.startsWith(\"docker/ci-tools/\"))\n\nSources:\n- push (GitHub, Forgejo): the payload's `commits[].added/modified/removed`. These lists can be cut short on large pushes, and a new branch (`before` all zeros) or a force push has no clean base. The compare API (`before...after`) is the complete source.\n- pull_request: the PR files API (GitHub `GET /repos/{o}/{r}/pulls/{n}/files`, paginated; Forgejo has an equivalent). One API call per PR event, made with the connection's credential.\n- tag, cron, manual, api, comment: no field. A `when:` that reads it there must get a defined answer.\n\nDecide:\n1. When the list is incomplete or missing, does a `when:` that reads it match? Proposed: treat the field as absent and have the trigger run, and log why, so a skipped build is never silent.\n2. Whether the list is stored with the Run (it is evidence for why the Run started), and its size cap.\n\nAcceptance: a push touching only `README.md` does not start a Run whose `when:` requires `docker/ci-tools/`; a push touching `docker/ci-tools/Dockerfile` does; a new-branch push and a PR on GitHub and Forgejo each behave as decided above; tests use recorded payloads, no network.","files":null}]}